      "text": "To expand the product \\((2x + 3)(x + 5)\\), we apply the distributive property, which states that \\( (a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd \\).\n\nHere, \\(a = 2x\\), \\(b = 3\\), \\(c = x\\), and \\(d = 5\\).\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n\\[\n(2x + 3)(x + 5) = (2x)(x) + (2x)(5) + (3)(x) + (3)(5)\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate each term:\n\n\\[\n(2x)(x) = 2x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n(2x)(5) = 10x\n\\]\n\\[\n(3)(x) = 3x\n\\]\n\\[\n(3)(5) = 15\n\\]\n\nNext, combine all the terms together:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15\n\\]\n\nCombine the like terms \\(10x\\) and \\(3x\\):\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 13x + 15\n\\]\n\nThus, the expanded form of \\((2x + 3)(x + 5)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2x^2 + 13x + 15}\n\\]",
