      "text": "Using the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials), we expand the expression as follows:\n\n\\[\n(2x+3)(x+5) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 5 + 3 \\cdot x + 3 \\cdot 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we simply multiply the coefficients:\n\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15\n\\]\n\nCombine the like terms:\n\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 13x + 15\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the expanded and simplified form of the given expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2x^2 + 13x + 15}\n\\]\n\nThis result can also be confirmed through the code solution. Let's implement this in Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, expand\n\n# Define the variable\nx = symbols('x')\n\n# Define the expression\nexpression = (2*x + 3)*(x + 5)\n\n# Expand the expression\nexpanded_expression = expand(expression)\nprint(expanded_expression)\n```",
